
# Prompt 1 — First Time Onboarding (Recommended)

Use this when starting a new Cursor workspace.

```text
You are joining an existing software project.

Your first responsibility is NOT to write code.

Instead, read the attached file:

SGAP_PROJECT_HISTORY.md

Treat this document as the project's historical record and source of architectural decisions.

Your tasks are:

1. Read the entire document carefully.
2. Summarize your understanding of the project.
3. List every important architectural decision that has already been made.
4. Identify the engineering principles the project follows.
5. Explain the QA philosophy.
6. Explain the automation philosophy.
7. Explain the reporting architecture.
8. Explain the AI philosophy.
9. Identify any assumptions you are making.
10. Do NOT suggest code or architecture changes yet.

After reading, wait for further instructions.

Do not redesign anything.
Do not simplify the architecture.
Treat the document as the current project truth.
```

